gvisor-windows is an unofficial port of gVisor (https://gvisor.dev) to Windows hosts.
It is not a Google project. gVisor is Copyright The gVisor Authors, Apache License 2.0.

Code borrowed from other projects is listed here with its origin:
- third_party/golang.org/x/sys: copy of golang.org/x/sys v0.48.0 (BSD-3-Clause, see its LICENSE). Its unix/*_shim_windows.go files are generated from the linux/amd64 files of the same version (ADR 0006).
- pkg/safecopy, pkg/sentry/pgalloc: the upstream gVisor test files (_test.go, from the commit the go branch was generated from) are copied and adapted only where they use Linux calls (Apache-2.0, same project; ADR 0009). The Windows vectored exception handler follows the Linux signal handler's register contract and the S5 spike (test/spikes/windows/s5).
- pkg/sentry/platform/winstub/x86asm: copy of the x86 decoder golang.org/x/arch/x86/x86asm (Copyright The Go Authors, BSD-3-Clause, see x86asm/LICENSE), taken from the Go toolchain's cmd/vendor copy (docs/results/1a-stub-prototype.md); the exact version was not recorded. Its AVX decoding was fixed locally (vzeroupper, vzeroall, endbr).
- Inherited from upstream gVisor and kept as is: pkg/shim/v1 and runsc/cgroup/cgroup_v2.go derive from containerd and runc (Apache-2.0, headers kept); pkg/safecopy and pkg/sentry/time assembly, pkg/sync/rwmutex_unsafe.go and some others derive from the Go runtime (BSD-3-Clause, headers kept).
